  "description": "bit Bmage: browser-side image processing for Blazor. Load, transform, annotate and export images on the user's device from strongly typed C#, with browser-native WebP and AVIF codecs, capability detection, IBrowserFile/clipboard/camera input and dependency injection wiring. Works in WebAssembly, Server and Auto render modes, and headlessly on a server through its browser-independent engine: pixel buffers, transforms, adjustments, filters, drawing, annotations, masks and selective edits, image, fill and adjustment layers with W3C blend modes, EXIF metadata, managed PNG/JPEG/BMP/GIF codecs, composable non-destructive pipelines and edits that save to JSON and replay on a server, spread over as many cores as you allow with identical pixels, with codec work in Web Workers in the browser and predictable, budgeted memory. Includes BmageEditor, a themeable, accessible, touch-friendly image editor component: crop, rotate, adjust, filter, draw, annotate, redact, undo/redo and export.",
